{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/120984","id":3994834326,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7uHFWW","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120984","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120984.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120984.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120984","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/120984/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/120984/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120984/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/c9ccf1cea9622179d66230d852f2a0bdca512ec7","number":120984,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Fix children's `parent_maximum_size_cache` unable to update twice in a frame","user":{"login":"StarryWorm","id":41305715,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxMzA1NzE1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/41305715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm","html_url":"https://github.com/StarryWorm","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\nFixes an issue whereby parent `Control` could not update their children's `parent_maximum_size_cache` more than once per frame.\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\nWhilst working on tests for containers for all the desired size behavior, I discovered that the `parent_maximum_size_cache` wouldn't update as intended when the following code was executed:\r\n```cpp\r\nparent->set_custom_maximum_size(Size2(100, 100));\r\nparent->set_propagate_maximum_size(false);\r\nSceneTree::get_singleton()->process(0);\r\nchild->get_combined_maximum_size() //  would return Size2(100, 100) instead of Size2(-1, -1)\r\n```\r\nBut it would work if the first two setters were flipped:\r\n```cpp\r\nparent->set_propagate_maximum_size(false);\r\nparent->set_custom_maximum_size(Size2(100, 100));\r\nSceneTree::get_singleton()->process(0);\r\nchild->get_combined_maximum_size() //  would return Size2(-1, -1)\r\n```\r\n\r\nTurns out the `&& child_control->data.maximum_size_valid` condition that I had copied from `update_minimum_size` when creating `update_maximum_size` was preventing the children's `parent_maximum_size_cache` from being updated more than once per frame.\r\n\r\n\r\nEdit: \r\nMRP [mrp-parent-cache.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/29858997/mrp-parent-cache.zip)\r\nRun the scene and press the big button, check the console output.","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":1732720779,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxNzMyNzIwNzc5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:gui","name":"topic:gui","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":15520464,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4A7NLQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/25","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengin